course: dictionary
lesson: 3575
title: Feudalism: land for loyalty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Feudalism was a system in medieval Europe. The king gave land to lords, and in return the lords gave him loyalty and soldiers. «The king gave land to lords, lords owed him soldiers, and peasants owed the lords work and part of their crops.» Each person owed something to the person above them.
explain: Think of feudalism as a pyramid. The king is at the top, then come barons and bishops, then knights, and peasants are at the bottom. Peasants, also called serfs, worked the lords' land. In return they got protection and a place to live, so the promise went both ways.
explain: Historians call this the feudal system, and a lord in it is a feudal lord. Feudal lords had castles, knights fought for them, and peasants had few rights. The word feudalism gives a name to the whole pattern, not just to one person.
fact: Feudalism was the system in medieval Europe, in the Middle Ages.
fact: The king gave land to lords, and the lords gave loyalty and soldiers back.
fact: Peasants, also called serfs, worked the lords' land for protection and a home.
fact: The Norman Conquest of 1066, led by William the Conqueror, brought this system to England.
fact: Similar systems existed in Japan too.
exercise: In feudalism, what did lords give the king in return for land? | *Loyalty and soldiers | Their land back every year | Gold coins for his treasury | Horses to race in the castle yard
exercise: Who was at the bottom of the feudal pyramid? | *Peasants | Knights | The king | Barons
exercise: What is a serf? | *A peasant who worked the lord's land | A lord who owns a castle | A messenger for the king | A knight in shining armour
test: In feudalism, what did peasants get in return for working the lord's land? | A seat at the king's table | A castle of their own | Gold | *Protection and a place to live
test: Who was at the very top of the feudal pyramid? | Knights | Lords | Peasants | *The king
exam: «The king gave land to lords, lords owed him soldiers.» What did lords owe the king in the feudal system? | Taxes of gold only | Their land back each year | Nothing at all | *Loyalty and soldiers
